            <ArticleTitle>FGF21 mimetic shows therapeutic promise.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>307-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2013.08.014</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(13)00340-9</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>FGF21 is a protein with multiple metabolic actions, currently a bright star beckoning on the metabolic disease therapeutic horizon. Gaich et al. (2013) present the first clinical efficacy trial for an FGF21 mimetic, finding robust lipid-lowering effects, some reduction in body weight, but surprisingly modest effects on glucose homeostasis.</AbstractText>
